**Given:**

Diagonals of the rhombus are 12 cm and 16 cm.

**Formula Used:**

Side of rhombus = sqrt{((d₁)/(2))² + ((d₂)/(2))²}

**Calculation:**

Given diagonals: d₁ = 12 cm and d₂ = 16 cm.

Half of the diagonals: (d₁)/(2) = 6 cm and (d₂)/(2) = 8 cm.

Side of rhombus = sqrt{6² + 8²}

Side of rhombus = sqrt{36 + 64}

Side of rhombus = sqrt{100}

Side of rhombus = 10 cm

**The length of the side of the rhombus is 10 cm.**
